1
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:06,090
Nice shot, Jakah!

2
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:06,920
Yeah!

3
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,890
Okay, I'm next!

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:10,950
Sooha!

5
00:00:10,950 --> 00:00:13,110
Shion! Guys!

6
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,770
You came to watch us practice?

7
00:00:15,770 --> 00:00:17,990
Yeah. The game's tomorrow, right?

8
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,450
How are you feeling?

9
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:20,600
Great!

10
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,640
You've been missing all your shots.

11
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:24,420
Huh?

12
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:25,750
Have I?

13
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,350
We'll be fine, though.

14
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:30,170
We'll win again, thanks to me.

15
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:32,310
I'll dedicate our victory to you.

16
00:00:32,310 --> 00:00:35,680
Huh? R-Really? Thanks.

17
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,510
Sooha, thanks for coming.

18
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:40,430
S-Sure.

19
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:47,190
I was born to protect you, 
and I have to keep protecting you.

20
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,650
I'll do my best, so I hope
 you'll cheer for me.

21
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:55,220
O-Okay. I really hope you win.

22
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:56,200
Yeah.

23
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,020
Hey.

24
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,580
It's dangerous for you to be here.

25
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,710
If you don't wanna get hurt, stay out.

26
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:05,670
Solon, are you worrying about me?

27
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:08,260
What? No!

28
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:10,490
Come on, let's practice!

29
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:11,280
Sure.

30
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:13,490
Okay, see you guys later.

31
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:18,970
- Vampire Lord -

32
00:01:28,210 --> 00:01:30,230
It's been 120 years.

33
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:32,670
How have you been, Director?

34
00:01:33,110 --> 00:01:35,610
Just fine, as you can see.

35
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:38,740
We thought you'd given up long ago.

36
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:41,660
We had no idea you were 
still looking for us.

37
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,580
I didn't come for you boys.

38
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:47,850
I'm pleased we ran into 
each other, though.

39
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,700
I see you all stayed together.

40
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,170
What's going on here?

41
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:54,950
We've finally met again.

42
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:57,170
I'll tell you boys, as well.

43
00:01:57,610 --> 00:02:01,230
You show up outta nowhere and 
want us to hear you out? Screw that!

44
00:02:01,770 --> 00:02:03,770
Don't listen to her!

45
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:05,350
We're not listening.

46
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:07,100
Get out of here.

47
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:12,440
We're not the kids you knew anymore.

48
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:20,060
There are more pressing matters right now.

49
00:02:33,750 --> 00:02:34,680
Khan!

50
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:36,730
Sorry for suddenly asking to meet.

51
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:37,840
Did something happen?

52
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,880
Well, actually...

53
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:43,160
I just really wanted 
to tell you something.

54
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:48,350
I love you, Sooha.

55
00:02:48,350 --> 00:02:49,320
What?

56
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:55,460
Werewolves fall in love for life.

57
00:02:56,530 --> 00:03:00,740
So I'll keep loving you until I die.

58
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:08,790
I'd be really happy if you cheered for
 me at our upcoming nightball game.

59
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:13,130
That's all I wanted to say.

60
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:19,130
I'll walk you back.

61
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:33,580
<i>At last, tonight is the nightball final!</i>

62
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:38,410
<i>Once again, Sunshine City School 
faces off against Decelis Academy!</i>

63
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:43,600
<i>I'll do my best, so I hope
 you'll cheer for me.</i>

64
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,910
<i>I'd be really happy if you cheered for me.</i>

65
00:03:46,910 --> 00:03:48,440
<i>What should I do?</i>

66
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:51,410
<i>I treasure my friendship 
with both of them.</i>

67
00:03:51,850 --> 00:03:53,920
<i>At least, that's what I thought.</i>

68
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,450
<i>But they're important to me as...</i>

69
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,550
I should focus on cheering right now!

70
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:06,470
<i>Will last year's champions, 
Decelis, repeat their success?</i>

71
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:09,710
<i>Or will Sunshine City get revenge?</i>

72
00:04:09,710 --> 00:04:13,230
<i>This red-hot game will 
be kicking off shortly!</i>

73
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:17,900
<i>Mahan, Rusland, Kamil...</i>

74
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:21,100
<i>You promised you'd be back.</i>

75
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:23,150
<i>No. I have to focus!</i>

76
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:25,410
We're going to win this game!

77
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,050
We'll easily beat you again this year!

78
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:28,870
Huh?

79
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:33,220
Sooha! Our team's supporters 
are sitting over there!

80
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:39,250
<i>Sooha, I promise I'll win for you.</i>

81
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:40,990
<i>What should I do?</i>

82
00:04:43,130 --> 00:04:46,300
<i>The game is about to begin!</i>

83
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:04,490
<i>Whoa! Will Decelis score here?!</i>

84
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,160
Jino! Over here!

85
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:08,990
Nice!

86
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:15,010
<i>Sunshine hits back! 
What a powerful tackle!</i>

87
00:05:11,490 --> 00:05:12,590
Shion!

88
00:05:15,010 --> 00:05:16,120
Nice, Khan!

89
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,960
Enzy!

90
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:22,840
Damn!

91
00:05:30,610 --> 00:05:32,660
<i>Decelis scores first!</i>

92
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:33,440
Nice, Heli.

93
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:33,980
Thanks.

94
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,140
Not bad!

95
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:38,060
Heli...

96
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:56,900
<i>The first half ends with 
Decelis leading by one!</i>

97
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:00,640
<i>That was rougher than I expected.</i>

98
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:02,750
<i>I hope nobody gets hurt.</i>

99
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:03,970
Sooha!

100
00:06:03,970 --> 00:06:06,590
Did you see me score earlier?

101
00:06:06,590 --> 00:06:08,840
Yeah! You were awesome!

102
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,990
Right?

103
00:06:09,990 --> 00:06:12,510
I scored our second point.

104
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:13,600
Sooha!

105
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:16,340
Our team's sitting over there!

106
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,560
Oh, um...

107
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,850
Sooha!

108
00:06:18,850 --> 00:06:22,940
We're trailing for now, but I swear
 we'll win, so cheer for me!

109
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:26,660
What? Sooha's rooting for us.

110
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:29,310
Sooha, our team's sitting on that side!

111
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:29,920
Hey!

112
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,700
Sooha's with us.

113
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:34,120
Sooha, are you having fun?

114
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,260
Heli?!

115
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,740
Cheer for us, okay?

116
00:06:40,930 --> 00:06:41,700
See you later.

117
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,250
That's all?

118
00:06:46,890 --> 00:06:47,950
Heli...

119
00:06:49,670 --> 00:06:50,510
Sooha.

120
00:06:52,670 --> 00:06:53,890
Do you have a moment?

121
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:58,910
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

122
00:06:58,950 --> 00:07:02,900
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

123
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,510
No...

124
00:07:08,470 --> 00:07:11,660
That's why I've been looking for you.

125
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,790
No!

126
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:27,130
<i>What? That was Sooha.</i>

127
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,550
<i>She's not there.</i>

128
00:07:33,170 --> 00:07:35,260
<i>She's gone. She's gone.</i>

129
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:36,830
<i>Sooha!</i>

130
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:46,360
Heli!

131
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,120
Are you okay?!

132
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:50,750
S-Sooha is...

133
00:07:50,750 --> 00:07:53,490
<i>I won't let them take it today!</i>

134
00:07:54,170 --> 00:07:56,030
<i>I have to win!</i>

135
00:07:57,940 --> 00:08:00,160
<i>Goal!</i>

136
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:02,730
<i>Sunshine City scores the goal 
they desperately wanted!</i>

137
00:08:00,490 --> 00:08:01,770
Yes!

138
00:08:02,110 --> 00:08:04,290
That was amazing, Khan!

139
00:08:02,730 --> 00:08:07,290
<i>Sunshine City gets revenge!</i>

140
00:08:04,290 --> 00:08:05,640
Damn.

141
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:07,290
We almost had them.

142
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:17,900
Sunshine! Sunshine! Sunshine!

143
00:08:11,650 --> 00:08:13,970
Heli, is something wrong?

144
00:08:13,970 --> 00:08:16,150
Something happened.

145
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:21,060
Sooha!

146
00:08:27,730 --> 00:08:29,570
Why were you with Sooha?

147
00:08:29,990 --> 00:08:31,530
Who took her?

148
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:36,260
Dardan, the First Vampire.

149
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,010
Dardan, the First Vampire? Who's that?

150
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:41,950
Could it be...

151
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:46,610
You really don't know anything, do you?

152
00:08:49,190 --> 00:08:52,920
Dardan was a chancellor of 
the ancient Vargr Kingdom.

153
00:08:53,630 --> 00:08:57,650
Though he was originally human, 
in pursuit of power,

154
00:08:57,650 --> 00:09:01,410
he turned himself into a vampire 
using a forbidden method.

155
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,360
That must be him.

156
00:09:04,690 --> 00:09:05,850
You've met him?

157
00:09:05,850 --> 00:09:10,870
Yeah. He attacked us with 
a horde of vampires.

158
00:09:10,870 --> 00:09:12,610
Who were those vampires with him?

159
00:09:13,210 --> 00:09:18,500
Lesser vampires created by Dardan.

160
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:22,760
Weak to sunlight and 
with no sense of reason,

161
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:25,120
they can't suppress 
their thirst for blood.

162
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,290
You understand, don't you?

163
00:09:28,290 --> 00:09:32,210
That you're different from those vampires.

164
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:37,350
You are vampire lords of 
the ancient Vargr Kingdom.

165
00:09:38,070 --> 00:09:40,310
Vampire lords?

166
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:46,390
Yes. You were also knights 
who served the princess.

167
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:49,900
You imprisoned us! 
We don't believe anything—

168
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,210
I wasn't imprisoning you.

169
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:55,990
I kept you at Vanfield to 
protect you from Dardan.

170
00:09:56,660 --> 00:10:01,670
Over a millennium ago, when Dardan's 
rebellion threatened the kingdom,

171
00:10:01,670 --> 00:10:06,690
the princess sent your souls into 
the distant future to protect you.

172
00:10:07,450 --> 00:10:13,670
However, you lost your memories 
and reverted to infancy.

173
00:10:14,210 --> 00:10:21,010
I tracked down every last one of you 
and protected you at Vanfield House.

174
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:26,310
Princess? Wait a minute.

175
00:10:26,310 --> 00:10:28,020
That princess...

176
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:29,270
Is she...

177
00:10:30,970 --> 00:10:33,410
Is she Sooha?

178
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:39,550
Yes. I tracked the princess's energy here.

179
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:43,030
You must've known 
instinctively, as well...

180
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:46,170
what your destinies are.

181
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:58,600
So, why did Dardan kidnap Sooha?

182
00:10:59,310 --> 00:11:01,010
The same reason he did in the past.

183
00:11:01,510 --> 00:11:05,140
Dardan is trying to acquire her power.

184
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:08,470
<i>Now everything will be mine.</i>

185
00:11:09,070 --> 00:11:11,190
The princess... Dardan...

186
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:12,660
I see.

187
00:11:41,990 --> 00:11:44,550
There you are, Your Highness.

188
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:46,760
Sir Heli.

189
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:49,320
The queen is calling for you.

190
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:51,850
It must be about... that.

191
00:11:53,110 --> 00:11:57,290
The prince of a neighboring 
kingdom proposed.

192
00:11:57,690 --> 00:12:02,340
Yes, I've heard. 
They say he's a great man.

193
00:12:02,670 --> 00:12:05,740
But I don't want to get married yet.

194
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:11,150
And I can't promise my life 
to someone I hardly know.

195
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:15,900
But I'm not allowed to choose who I love.

196
00:12:16,870 --> 00:12:22,130
I'm sure you'll meet someone you can 
love from the bottom of your heart.

197
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:27,680
Perhaps I should tell Mother how I...

198
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,760
Your Highness!

199
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:32,210
What's wrong?

200
00:12:33,230 --> 00:12:35,980
Thank you, Sir Heli.

201
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:40,980
You're always rescuing me.

202
00:12:43,310 --> 00:12:46,580
It's my job to protect you, Your Highness.

203
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:03,190
You look lovely as always 
today, Princess Selen.

204
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,760
Will you be accepting 
the prince's proposal?

205
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:11,210
Chancellor Dardan, 
I respectfully declined his offer.

206
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:13,660
That's good news.

207
00:13:14,510 --> 00:13:17,190
I didn't think you'd do as I wanted.

208
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:19,230
It's none of your business!

209
00:13:19,530 --> 00:13:22,730
I agree with you, Princess Selen.

210
00:13:22,730 --> 00:13:25,110
I'm opposed to political marriages.

211
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:28,450
You eavesdropped on me?!

212
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:32,450
I just naturally hear your voice.

213
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:33,920
Why?

214
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:36,000
Because I'm always listening for it.

215
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,290
How rude!

216
00:13:38,670 --> 00:13:40,180
Rude?

217
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:43,670
Because I'm not royalty?

218
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:47,090
So status <i>is</i> important to you!

219
00:13:47,090 --> 00:13:48,220
Unhand me!

220
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:53,470
How can I make your heart mine—

221
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:55,430
Dardan!

222
00:13:55,720 --> 00:14:00,060
The next time you disrespect the 
princess like that, you'll pay dearly!

223
00:14:06,290 --> 00:14:08,610
He's unbelievable.

224
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:11,810
Your Highness!

225
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:18,060
Selen! Selen, please hold on!

226
00:14:20,770 --> 00:14:22,340
It is as we feared.

227
00:14:22,850 --> 00:14:23,980
What is this?

228
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:27,690
I believe it's due to the royal 
bloodline's shamanistic powers.

229
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:33,400
Princess Selen's powers are the 
strongest the kingdom has ever seen.

230
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:36,540
Her body can no longer withstand them.

231
00:14:37,530 --> 00:14:39,580
At this rate, she'll die.

232
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:43,460
There's only one way to keep her alive.

233
00:14:44,110 --> 00:14:47,900
We'll use the blood of the kingdom's 
treasured ancient wolf god...

234
00:14:48,550 --> 00:14:50,850
The blood of Vargr.

235
00:14:59,450 --> 00:15:00,440
Selen!

236
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:06,270
<i>What is this? I feel so warm...</i>

237
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:11,970
Your Highness, you are Selen, 
the princess who carries shaman's blood.

238
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:16,790
I, Vargr the wolf god, 
shall grant you strength.

239
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,850
You're Vargr?

240
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:29,400
Selen, you're awake!

241
00:15:30,070 --> 00:15:32,670
Thank goodness. You're all right now.

242
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:37,350
Mother, I met the god Vargr.

243
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:41,920
O great Vargr, thank you.

244
00:15:45,190 --> 00:15:49,170
One Year Later

245
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:52,590
Mother! Mother!

246
00:15:53,590 --> 00:15:57,580
Selen, don't be so sad.

247
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:03,060
You know this is the only way.

248
00:16:03,060 --> 00:16:04,330
Mother...

249
00:16:05,150 --> 00:16:10,570
Now that he's become First Vampire, 
Dardan is trying to take over the kingdom.

250
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:17,130
The werewolves aided us, 
but their numbers were too great.

251
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:24,260
So you gave them your blood...

252
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:38,260
and created new vampire lords.

253
00:16:39,830 --> 00:16:43,020
Please, work together...

254
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:49,660
to protect this nation from Dardan.

255
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:55,710
But I'm just...

256
00:16:55,710 --> 00:16:58,780
By drinking Vargr's blood,

257
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:05,300
you acquired the power of the ancient 
wolf god and became a vampire queen.

258
00:17:05,950 --> 00:17:11,230
Selen, take my shamanistic power.

259
00:17:12,190 --> 00:17:17,920
My power has already been 
sealed in the moon altar.

260
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,220
Mother...

261
00:17:19,450 --> 00:17:26,690
Selen, if I die, you must hold a 
coronation ceremony at the moon altar,

262
00:17:26,690 --> 00:17:30,480
break the seal,
 receive the queen's power,

263
00:17:31,310 --> 00:17:34,600
and become the most 
powerful queen of all time.

264
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,610
Don't worry, Your Majesty.

265
00:17:39,010 --> 00:17:44,000
I shall claim that power 
and rule this kingdom well.

266
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:45,710
Dardan!

267
00:17:45,710 --> 00:17:50,620
Princess Selen, I didn't want to do this.

268
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:55,550
I simply wanted your love, but you 
wouldn't so much as glance my way.

269
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:56,970
Step back!

270
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,390
Marge!

271
00:18:02,470 --> 00:18:07,600
So the only way to make you mine 
is to take you and crush you.

272
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,030
Protect the princess!

273
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,580
Heli, get the princess!

274
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,460
Your Highness, are you all right?

275
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,830
Dardan, you bastard!

276
00:18:30,830 --> 00:18:32,200
Stay out of my way!

277
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,460
Sir Heli!

278
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:41,090
You also love the princess, 
so you must understand.

279
00:18:41,090 --> 00:18:45,220
You alone should admit I'm right.

280
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:50,600
Bastard...

281
00:18:58,950 --> 00:19:02,230
Now everything will be mine.

282
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:05,120
Princess! To the moon altar!

283
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:06,490
You must hurry!

284
00:19:07,670 --> 00:19:09,550
Your Highness! Your Highness!

285
00:19:24,630 --> 00:19:26,110
Marge, your back!

286
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:29,000
Hurry... The coronation...

287
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:31,190
I can't!

288
00:19:31,190 --> 00:19:35,740
I can't sacrifice everyone 
to become queen!

289
00:19:38,650 --> 00:19:41,330
Marge, I have a request.

290
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,520
I'm going to return to the palace

291
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:47,930
and send the knights' souls 
into the distant future.

292
00:19:48,410 --> 00:19:54,810
When the time comes, 
please find them and protect them.

293
00:19:54,810 --> 00:19:55,920
Your Highness...

294
00:20:04,650 --> 00:20:06,180
You'll pay for this!

295
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:10,350
For you, there's no limit 
to how cruel I can be.

296
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:16,690
Stay down!

297
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:25,450
Your Highness!

298
00:20:28,730 --> 00:20:37,580
Sir Heli, you've saved me 
from danger so many times...

299
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:41,880
without any fear or hesitation.

300
00:20:42,390 --> 00:20:48,570
I know you've been hiding something...

301
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:54,390
because I've been hiding the same thing.

302
00:20:55,670 --> 00:20:58,880
Next time, please...

303
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:02,570
Let us be our true selves.

304
00:21:25,370 --> 00:21:31,290
Dardan tried to take Sooha's shamanistic 
powers and the power of Vargr.

305
00:21:32,290 --> 00:21:33,430
Yes.

306
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:38,060
I see. That legend...

307
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:40,390
It was about us.

308
00:23:34,030 --> 00:23:39,890
<i>Next time, Episode 9: 
"Misty Moon: The Black Mist of Railgun."</i>

309
00:23:36,950 --> 00:23:40,250
- The Black Mist of Railgun -

